  {
    "index": 3,
    "hash": "96W8HSA5b5ZhehWowrrt9PWd+Qs=",
    "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-19T11:28:57.038Z",
    "action": {
      "type": "SET_CONTENT",
      "input": {
        "content": "Info Support is described as the best-evidenced Dutch firm in the set and a genuine custom house, meaning nothing of its own occupies the application layer and there is no internal product to displace. On the two structural questions the screen cares about \u2014 evidence quality and an empty app-layer slot \u2014 it scores as well as any Dutch lead.\n\nThe offset is culture rather than capability. It is a .NET and Azure house, which costs it on technical affinity; its stack was not otherwise researched. Affinity matters because a first partner's engineers have to be able to read and extend what gets built, and a bench whose daily language is C# will experience a TypeScript-based stack as a new thing to learn rather than as an extension of what it already does.\n\nAt 500+ people it is also above the size where one conversation decides. The result is a strong lead held at priority 3 for reasons that are about friction rather than doubt.\n\n---\n\n## Leads sharing this finding (1)\n\n**3 \u00b7 later**\n- Info Support (NL \u00b7 500+)\n\nVerbatim research text this claim was extracted from:\n\n> Best-evidenced Dutch firm and a genuine custom house with an empty app-layer slot, but a .NET culture costs it on technical affinity.",
        "updatedAt": "2026-08-19T11:28:57.038386Z"
      },
      "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-19T11:28:57.038389Z"
    }
  },
